  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_021 (acc=0.629, F1=0.599) with multiprofile + pca_n2000 + ViT-L + avgpool + concat. The jump from singleprofile (config_009, 0.527) to multiprofile+avgpool (config_010, 0.619) was the largest gain observed, but aggregation has only been tested as avgpool. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) can further improve over simple average pooling when combining multiple profiles. Question tested: config_045 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other factors constant (pca_n2000, ViT-L, multiprofile, concat), giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_021. Why this is the best next experiment: Aggregation is a fundamental design choice for how multiprofile information is combined, and the potential gain from a learned (transformer) aggregation over a fixed (avgpool) one is a major open question. Isolating this single factor on the current best configuration maximizes information per experiment and directly informs whether to invest further in transformer-based aggregation or confirm avgpool sufficiency."
}

